<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela seeks use of CANTV sale for debt fund.</title>
<headline>Venezuela seeks use of CANTV sale for debt fund.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuela's cabinet of ministers approved Wednesday a 287 billion bolivar ($610 million) spending request, backed by revenues from the forthcoming CANTV privatisation, that will be used to pay off domestic and foreign debt, Ministers said.</p>
<p>&quot;This additional spending credit will be solely backed by proceeds from the CANTV sale,&quot; Information Minister Fernando Egana told reporters.</p>
<p>The cabinet also approved a further 126 billion bolivars spending request, also to pay-off debt, and another 30 billion bolivar request that will be used to pay pending public worker salary bonuses.</p>
<p>-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600</p>
</text>
